  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "htmlParseChunk",
    "file": "libxml2/HTMLparser.c",
    "description": "Use-after-free is caused by htmlParseChunk saving parser input pointers as offsets before calling xmlParserInputBufferPush, then restoring them onto ctxt->input->buf->buffer after push. During push, xmlCharEncInput can grow/realloc the active buffer (xmlBufGrowInternal), freeing the old memory and updating input->base/cur to the new allocation. htmlParseChunk then calls xmlBufSetInputBaseCur with stale pre-push offsets against the possibly replaced buffer, reintroducing dangling base/cur pointers. A later error path (htmlParseErr -> __xmlRaiseError -> xmlReportError -> xmlParserPrintFileContextInternal) dereferences input->cur/base and reads freed memory.",
    "conditions": "Triggered in HTML push parsing when input contains markup that causes encoding switching (e.g., meta charset handling) so ctxt->input->buf has encoder/raw paths active, and a subsequent chunk push causes buffer growth/reallocation in xmlCharEncInput. After this realloc, htmlParseChunk restores input base/cur from stale saved values, and then any parser error reporting that prints file context accesses input->cur/base, producing UAF. The fuzz harness html.c drives this via repeated htmlParseChunk calls with attacker-controlled bytes."
  },
